[[Image:The Moon, Mars and Venus.jpg|thumb|225px|Mond und '''Abendstern''' — Moon and '''evening star''']]

===Etymology===
Compound of {{compound|Abend|Stern|t1=evening|t2=star|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈaːbn̩tˌʃtɛʁn]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Abendstern.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Abendsternes|gen2=Abendsterns|Abendsterne}}

# {{lb|de|astronomy}} [[evening star|Evening star]]; the [[planet]] [[Venus]] as seen in the [[west]]ern [[sky]] in the [[evening]].
# {{lb|de|astronomy}} [[evening star|Evening star]]; any [[star]] (or planet, [[anciently]] thought to be a star) [[seen]] in the [[evening]], ''especially'' the [[planet]]s [[Mercury]] and [[Jupiter]].

